on under the integral is unbounded as we approach the *lower* integration limit from any point that lies in the interval $x\\in (1,4):$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\to \\infty \\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to {1}^{+}\n$$\n\nWe can attempt to evaluate this integral by integrating $f(x)$ over the interval $x\\in [a,4]$ and taking the limit as $a\\to {1}^{+}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to {1}^{+}}({\\int }_{a}^{4}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-142389/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a83d52a4-6f69-5607-8753-e96c13bd7209"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-142389"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-141131/selection/2f7268ea7181d6cafb508fd642cf477d29a77d7108981a5b990f13e62b557a10" :answer/id #uuid "fb395732-74e6-5076-b471-849d7a9912de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{b\\to {0}^{-}}({\\int }_{-4}^{b}\\frac{1}{16-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141131/selection/431848d7ce3de87e635abdf2c695042f7aff24ea36055b51786020c8f80f42ac" :answer/id #uuid "0ad28b0d-d3e2-5ebb-805b-cd0f3aab5a6b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{b\\to {0}^{+}}({\\int }_{b}^{4}\\frac{1}{16-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141131/selection/49707a811423e07c40aa655502f72af1da9de674a1e7bab55ae4bb524c876b79" :answer/id #uuid "1cac2c6c-3348-5090-86cb-04404f1c8831" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{b\\to -\\infty }({\\int }_{b}^{4}\\frac{1}{16-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141131/selection/20cc48f8436555c3295566dfff7a4742858c8a28b3ea45130110585c89a7e7b8" :answer/id #uuid "c9248410-e441-5c03-a317-5057ddd33e3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{b\\to {4}^{-}}({\\int }_{0}^{b}\\frac{1}{16-{x}^{2}}\\,\\tex