9b353d5dc4e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-82701/selection/4616cd89bd77a29209600f7ff795bd9d358be9bf887e063a8d7152276d232525" "q-82701/selection/125f65a9faab814ef6898de7efc00a67e9cefe57d03bcda35e8c65ed57006963" "q-82701/selection/ee0630ba72c0c80a1917e1543e4ffb02b26d7c28b4845e1e78c337f1acb1f9c0" "q-82701/selection/c41c782e6dbd5c8f69e2a24666017b889f0d47356c48ec76c7a4ad6bb8c51274" "q-82701/selection/6460c973e724cfdd183cc5fa4cf37251ba18fceaeb8ed231c5419b353d5dc4e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-82701" :question/id #uuid "f2da8aa5-7ca5-5be0-be72-5709a0d5972c" :question/math-academy-id "q-82701" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to \n${\\int }_{-2}^{3}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{{x}^{3}+8}?$" :question/worked-solution "This is an improper integral of the second kind because the function under the integral is unbounded as we approach the *lower* integration limit from any point that lies in the interval $x\\in (-2,3):$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}+8}\\to \\infty \\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to (-2)^{+}\n$$\n\nWe can attempt to evaluate this integral by integrating $f(x)$ over the interval $x\\in [a,3]$ and taking the limit as $a\\to (-2)^{+}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{3}\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}+8}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to (-2)^{+}}({\\int }_{a}^{3}\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}+8}\\,\\text{d}x)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-82701/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a83d52a4-6f69-5607-8753-e96c13bd7209"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-82701"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-49889/selection/fe633ac6ae33a76eb5f84f7dde66ed853f94dba88ef7c45de28325072969a050" :answer/id #uuid "09d1d397-fb03-5b92-ba8e-b40d728f29bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{a\\to +\\infty }({\\int }_{-1}^{a}\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}+1}\\,\\text{d}x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49889/selection/7d6fbe626708688bfac062ca1b3c825af0d46cdd4e8f40